  "slug": "regulation-reveals-fddd",
  "summary": "Recent studies link tRNA pools, ribosome composition and nutrient-dependent ribosome pausing to translation regulation beyond transcript abundance.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that translational output is shaped by tRNA supply and ribosome state, not transcript abundance alone. Single-cell tRNA sequencing (sctRNA-seq) jointly profiles mRNA and tRNA abundance, linking tRNA-dependent control to cell identity. In beta-cells, high glucose reduces RPLP1 on translating ribosomes, impairing insulin translation and secretion. MYC promotes pre-tRNA maturation to expand the mature tRNA pool during re-entry into proliferation in HepaRG cells. In budding yeast, nutrient repletion engages sequence-dependent ribosome pausing and tRNA charging changes. A labelled protein ratio normalization for nascent proteome SILAC data preserves global translation changes masked by median normalization, revealing distinct targets of eIF4A1/2 and of their inhibitor silvestrol. Together, these studies position translation as a dynamically reprogrammed control layer.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
